<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-BALTIC BEVERAGES APPOINTS NEW MANAGER.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-BALTIC BEVERAGES APPOINTS NEW MANAGER.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baltic Beverage Holding, which has a 75 percent stake in Estonia's Saku Brewery , has appointed Christian Ramm-Schmidt as its new managing director, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Ramm-Schmidt, currently the managing director of Fazer Confectionery, will take up his position on October 6, succeeding Henrik Therman, who will retire, the company added in a statement.</p>
<p>Baltic Beverages Holding AB is a joint-venture company owned equally by Finland's Hartwall and the Swedish-Norwegian company Pripps Ringnes.</p>
<p>It also has majority stakes in leading breweries in Latvia, Lithuania and Russia.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
